(1, 1, 1, 'What is the main topic of this passage?', 'The method by which one-celled organisms reproduce', 'A comparison between mitosis and meiosis', 'Meiosis, the process by which identical cells are produced', NULL, 'B', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(2, 2, 2, 'This author\'s main purpose in writing is to', 'discuss the significance of mining in Canada and the United States', 'show the influence of the Klondike gold strike on the creative arts', 'point out the impact of the Klondike gold strike', NULL, 'C', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(3, 3, 3, 'The passage mainly concerns the', 'basic principles of building keystone arches', 'uses of arches in modern architecture', 'role of scaffolding in building keystone arches', NULL, 'A', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(4, 4, 4, 'What is the author\'s main purpose in this passage?', 'To show that a manufacturer\'s negligence can be shown by direct evidence only', 'To define circumstantial evidence and show its usefulness', 'To demonstrate that circumstantial evidence can be very useful in science', NULL, 'B', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(5, 5, 5, 'What is the main topic of this passage?', 'The structure of government', 'The provisions of an important law', 'The establishment of schools in the NorthwestTerritory', NULL, 'B', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(6, 6, 6, 'What does the passage mainly discuss?', 'How the Depression hurt U.S. motels', 'The impact of transcontinental highways', 'Two decades of growth for the motel industry', NULL, 'C', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(7, 7, 7, 'What is the author\'s main point?', 'Old proverbs often contain important truths.', 'Trees with shallow roots are more likely to avoid lightning than those with deep roots.', 'The deeper a tree\'s roots, the safer it is during a thunderstorm.', NULL, 'B', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(8, 8, 8, 'What is the main idea of this passage?', 'Alternative histories describe worlds in which history has taken another course.', 'Alternative histories are a type of historical novel.', 'Science fiction writers have accurately predicted certain actual scientific developments.', NULL, 'A', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(9, 9, 9, 'Why did the author write this passage?', 'To prove that Wilkinson\'s invention was based on Maudsley\'s', 'To demonstrate the importance of mass production to American society', 'To show the usefulness of Wilkinson\'s invention', NULL, 'C', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(10, 10, 10, 'The main idea of this passage is that', 'inventors have been inspired by toys to build new forms of transportation', 'toy automobiles and airplanes were very popular in the early 1900\'s', 'toy design has followed developments in transportation', NULL, 'C', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(11, 11, 1, 'The primary purpose of this passage is to', 'trace the development of American folk music', 'explain the oral tradition', 'contrast the styles of folk musicians', 'point out the influence of social issues on "urban" folk music', 'A', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(12, 12, 2, 'The main topic of this passage is', 'effective communication', 'the special language of psychology', 'two definitions of the word anxiety', 'the jargon of science', 'B', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(13, 14, 4, 'What is the main idea of this passage?', 'After initial success, off-Broadway theater began to decline.', 'Off-Broadway theaters produced many hit commercial plays.', 'Theaters on Broadway were not well equipped.', 'Off-Broadway plays were highly creative.', 'A', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(14, 14, 5, 'The paragraph that follows this passage most likely deals with', 'the help off-Broadway producers provided directors, playwrights, and performers', 'methods off-Broadway theaters used to cope with rising prices', 'the development of off-off-Broadway theater', 'the decline of Broadway theater', 'C', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(15, 15, 6, 'What is the main idea of this passage?', 'Each of the cultural areas was dominated by one of the language families.', 'The Zuni language is closely related to the Algonquin language.', 'There is considerable diversity in the size and the number of languages in language families of the North American Indians.', 'Contact with Europeans had an extraordinary effect on the languages of the Indian tribes of North America.', 'C', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(16, 16, 7, 'The main purpose of the passage is to', 'present a brief history of American journalism', 'outline certain developments in mid-19th-century journalism', 'explain the importance of the steam cylinder rotary press', 'present some biographical information about Richard Hoe', 'B', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(17, 16, 8, 'What is the most probable topic of the paragraph preceding this one?', 'Other types of rotary presses', 'Alternatives to using wire services', 'Newspapers that concentrated on politics', 'Other developments in journalism', 'D', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(18, 16, 9, 'The tone of the passage could best be described as', 'objective', 'optimistic', 'angry', 'humorous', 'A', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(19, 17, 10, 'Which of the following best expresses the main idea of this passage?', 'If a major earthquake strikes Los Angeles, it will probably damage San Francisco as well.', 'The New Madrid earthquake of 1811 was felt in Boston and Toronto.', 'The geology of the western United States is much more complex than that of the East.', 'Earthquakes travel farther in the East than in the West.', 'D', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(20, 18, 11, 'With which of the following statements would the author probably agree?', 'Children lack the ability to concentrate.', 'Young children have a much greater curiosity than adult scientists do.', 'The first few years of school are the most important ones for most children.', 'Adults can use children\'s intense curiosity to help children learn more.', 'D', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(21, 18, 12, 'The paragraph following this one most likely deals with', 'ways in which adults can help children learn by stimulating their curiosity', 'the learning habits of children over the age of four', 'the methods adult scientists use to study the curiosity of young children', 'ways in which adults can become as curious as children about their environments', 'A', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(22, 19, 13, 'The passage mainly discusses', 'U.S. cities in the late nineteenth century', 'the idealism of college graduates', 'settlement houses in the late 1800\'s and early 1900\'s', 'the life of several American social reformers', 'C', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(23, 20, 14, 'The author\'s attitude toward Isadora Duncan could best be described as one of', 'displeasure', 'admiration', 'compassion', 'amazement', 'B', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(24, 20, 15, 'Which of the following best describes the organization of the passage?', 'The author first discusses Isadora Duncan\'s style of dance and then her life history.', 'The first paragraph deals with Isadora Duncan\'s role as a teacher, the second her role as a performer.', 'The author first discusses Isadora Duncan\'s shortcomings and then her positive points.', 'First there is an analysis of Isadora Duncan\'s influences and then of her lasting contributions to dance.', 'A', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
(25, 21, 16, 'Which of the following statements best summarizes the author\'s attitude toward medieval alchemists?', 'Although they were all fakes, they made important contributions to science.', 'Their discovery of the philosopher\'s stone was more important than the achievements of modern chemists.', 'Although their theories were sound, they lacked the equipment needed to accomplish their goals.', 'They were unable to realize their goals, but they helped prepare the way for modern chemistry.', 'D', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', '2026-03-12 00:54:24', NULL, NULL),
