(632, 18, 2, '_________ "nova" means new, novas are actually stars that have existed for a long time and suddenly flare into brilliance.', 'That', 'Why', 'Although', 'It is', 'C', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Kalimat menunjukkan kontras antara makna nama "nova" dan kenyataan bintang. "Although" (meskipun) sebagai konjungsi konsesif adalah yang tepat. Pilihan A membentuk klausa subjek yang tidak sesuai konteks; pilihan B tidak bermakna; pilihan D tidak membentuk hubungan yang benar.'),
(633, 18, 3, 'Because Mars is farther from the Sun than _________, Mars takes longer to complete a revolution.', 'Earth is', 'is from Earth', 'what is Earth', 'is it Earth', 'A', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Perbandingan yang benar menggunakan struktur paralel: "farther than Earth is." Pilihan B, C, D memiliki struktur yang tidak paralel atau susunan kata yang terbalik.'),
(634, 18, 4, 'A social system is _________ of social relations that draws the behavior of its members toward the core values of the group.', 'a complex network', 'how a complex network', 'a complex network and', 'a network that is complex', 'A', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '"a complex network of social relations" adalah komplemen nomina yang tepat setelah is. Pilihan B membentuk klausa tidak lengkap; pilihan C menggunakan and tanpa predikat sesudahnya; pilihan D salah karena of perlu didahului kata benda sederhana.'),
(635, 18, 5, 'Bubbles, flaws, and other irregularities diffuse the light that passes through stained glass, _________ the glass sparkle.', 'which making', 'and making', 'making', 'to making', 'C', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '"making" berperan sebagai participial phrase hasil (result participle): "...making the glass sparkle." Pilihan A salah (seharusnya which makes); pilihan B tidak natural; pilihan D salah (tidak ada to + gerund).'),
(636, 18, 6, 'Fog is common near _________ inland bodies of water and along coasts in temperate zones.', 'there are large', 'large', 'either large', 'where large', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Diperlukan adjektiva sederhana untuk memodifikasi "inland bodies of water": "near large inland bodies of water." Pilihan A salah secara struktur; pilihan C menggunakan either yang tidak cocok dengan and; pilihan D adalah klausa tidak lengkap.'),
(637, 18, 7, 'The portrayal of everyday life in the objects of folk art makes it _________ valuable source of history.', 'and a', 'so that a', 'a', 'is a', 'C', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Setelah "makes it" diperlukan artikel + noun phrase sebagai complement: "makes it a valuable source." Pilihan A dan B membentuk kalimat tidak sempurna; pilihan D redundan dengan verba ganda.'),
(638, 18, 8, '_______ by the United States government\'s Bureau of Labor Statistics, the Consumer Price Index compares current costs of goods and services with past costs.', 'To prepare', 'As it prepared', 'When preparation', 'Prepared', 'D', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Kalimat utama sudah lengkap; bagian pembuka perlu menjadi participial phrase: "Prepared by..." Pilihan A (infinitive tujuan – salah konteks), B (klausa yang redundan), C (frase nomina – tidak bisa menjadi modifier kalimat).'),
(639, 18, 9, '_________ carries the genes, which determine the hereditary characteristics of the cell or organism.', 'The chromosome', 'The chromosome that', 'Whereas the chromosome', 'There is a chromosome', 'A', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '"The chromosome" adalah subjek yang tepat untuk verb "carries." Pilihan B membuat relative clause tanpa main verb; pilihan C membuat klausa subordinat tanpa main clause; pilihan D menghasilkan "There is a chromosome carries" yang tidak gramatikal.'),
(640, 18, 10, '_________ directly with most metals to form compounds called carbides.', 'Carbon reacting', 'Carbon reacts', 'The reaction of carbon', 'When carbon reacts', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '"Carbon reacts" membentuk kalimat lengkap dengan subjek dan predikat. Pilihan A adalah fragment (tidak ada main verb); pilihan C adalah noun phrase tanpa verb; pilihan D adalah klausa subordinat.'),
(641, 18, 11, 'Meteorites are slowed down by Earth\'s atmosphere, but if they are moving _________, they can form a crater on impact.', 'enough fast', 'fast enough', 'so fast enough', 'enough are fast', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Urutan yang benar adalah adverbia + enough: "moving fast enough." Pilihan A memiliki urutan terbalik; pilihan C redundan; pilihan D salah secara total.'),
(642, 18, 12, 'Located at the upper end of each________ an adrenal gland, an integral part of the endocrine system.', 'kidney which is', 'kidney is', 'kidney being', 'kidney', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Ini adalah kalimat terbalik (inverted sentence): "Located at the upper end of each kidney is an adrenal gland." Pilihan A membuat relative clause tanpa main verb; pilihan C adalah fragment; pilihan D tidak lengkap.'),
(643, 18, 13, 'About 75 percent of all cadmium is used for cadmium plating of _________ such as iron and steel.', 'easily corroded metals', 'metals are easily corroded', 'corroded metals that easily', 'how easily metals corroded', 'A', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '"easily corroded metals" adalah noun phrase sederhana yang tepat sebagai objek dari "of." Pilihan B tidak bisa menggunakan "are" tanpa "that"; pilihan C dan D salah secara struktur.'),
(644, 18, 14, 'An atom is a basic structural unit of matter, the smallest particle of an element _________ into chemical combination.', 'that can enter', 'can it enter', 'when entering it can', 'that enters can', 'A', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '"that can enter" adalah relative clause yang tepat untuk memodifikasi "the smallest particle." Pilihan B salah secara susunan kata; pilihan C memiliki urutan kata yang salah; pilihan D tidak gramatikal.'),
(645, 18, 15, 'All the major cities of the United States, ________ the cities of the Great Lakes and the Gulf of Mexico, began as centers of trade.', 'and to include', 'which including', 'included', 'including', 'D', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '"including" berfungsi sebagai participial phrase: "including the cities of the Great Lakes and the Gulf of Mexico." Pilihan A tidak bermakna; pilihan B salah (seharusnya which include); pilihan C mengubah makna kalimat menjadi tidak tepat.'),
(646, 18, 16, 'Settled by English Puritans in 1630, Boston became _________ .', 'the capital of the Massachusetts Bay Colony', 'the Massachusetts Bay Colony its capital', 'it was the capital of the Massachusetts Bay Colony', 'so that the capital of the Massachusetts Bay Colony', 'A', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Setelah "became" diperlukan noun phrase sebagai komplemen: "the capital of the Massachusetts Bay Colony." Pilihan B memiliki double subject (its capital); pilihan C membentuk run-on sentence; pilihan D tidak gramatikal.'),
(647, 18, 17, 'The Milky Way is <span class="error-option" data-label="A">a flat spiral galaxy</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="B">who</span> contains <span class="error-option" data-label="C">an estimated 100 billion</span> stars, <span class="error-option" data-label="D">including the Sun</span>.', 'a flat spiral galaxy', 'who', 'an estimated 100 billion', 'including the Sun', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '"who" digunakan untuk orang, sedangkan "galaxy" adalah benda. Relative pronoun yang benar adalah "that" atau "which": "a flat spiral galaxy that contains..."'),
(648, 18, 18, 'The piano <span class="error-option" data-label="A">as it is known today</span> represents <span class="error-option" data-label="B">a long series of experiments</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="C">extend back</span> to the year 1711, <span class="error-option" data-label="D">or perhaps even earlier</span>.', 'as it is known today', 'a long series of experiments', 'extend back', 'or perhaps even earlier', 'C', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Setelah "experiments" diperlukan participial phrase: "a long series of experiments extending back to..." atau klausa relatif "that extend back." Bentuk "extend" tanpa modifier salah secara gramatikal.'),
(649, 18, 19, 'Climate is <span class="error-option" data-label="A">the primarily force</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="B">that distinguishes</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="C">one biome</span>, or major terrestrial region, <span class="error-option" data-label="D">from another</span>.', 'the primarily force', 'that distinguishes', 'one biome', 'from another', 'A', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '"primarily" adalah adverbia, tetapi di sini digunakan untuk memodifikasi noun "force." Adjektiva yang benar adalah "primary": the primary force.'),
(650, 18, 20, 'Prehistoric villagers tended <span class="error-option" data-label="A">to work harder</span>, <span class="error-option" data-label="B">suffer from more diseases</span>, and eat <span class="error-option" data-label="C">the poorer diet</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="D">than nomadic hunters did</span>.', 'to work harder', 'suffer from more diseases', 'the poorer diet', 'than nomadic hunters did', 'C', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Dalam perbandingan ini, "poorer diet" menggunakan artikel tak tentu "a", bukan "the", karena bukan diet spesifik yang sudah disebut sebelumnya. Bentuk benar: eat a poorer diet than...');
INSERT INTO `toefl_structure_questions` (`id`, `section_id`, `question_number`, `question_text`, `option_a`, `option_b`, `option_c`, `option_d`, `correct_answer`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `explanation`) VALUES
(651, 18, 21, 'A major Canadian city, Montreal is <span class="error-option" data-label="A">second only to Paris</span> as <span class="error-option" data-label="B">the most largest</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="C">French-speaking city</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="D">in the world</span>.', 'second only to Paris', 'the most largest', 'French-speaking city', 'in the world', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '"most largest" adalah bentuk superlatif ganda yang salah. Karena "large" adalah adjektiva satu suku kata, superlatif yang benar adalah "largest" saja, bukan "most largest."'),
(652, 18, 22, '<span class="error-option" data-label="A">Archaeological and geological excavations</span> indicate <span class="error-option" data-label="B">which</span> a primitive type of corn <span class="error-option" data-label="C">was used as food</span> in North America <span class="error-option" data-label="D">at least 7,000 years ago</span>.', 'Archaeological and geological excavations', 'which', 'was used as food', 'at least 7,000 years ago', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Setelah verb "indicate" dibutuhkan klausa nomina dengan konjungsi "that": indicate that a primitive type of corn... Kata "which" tidak bisa memperkenalkan noun clause.'),
(653, 18, 23, 'The major component of the sedimentary rock called shale is clay, <span class="error-option" data-label="A">an earthy, fine-grained material</span> consisting <span class="error-option" data-label="B">primary</span> of <span class="error-option" data-label="C">a particular group</span> of <span class="error-option" data-label="D">crystalline minerals</span>.', 'an earthy, fine-grained material', 'primary', 'a particular group', 'crystalline minerals', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '"primary" adalah adjektiva, tetapi di sini dibutuhkan adverbia untuk memodifikasi verb "consisting": consisting primarily of... Bentuk adverbia yang benar adalah "primarily."'),
(654, 18, 24, 'Copper was <span class="error-option" data-label="A">the first metal</span> used by humans and is second only to iron <span class="error-option" data-label="B">into</span> its utility <span class="error-option" data-label="C">through the ages</span>.', 'the first metal', 'into', 'through the ages', 'used by humans', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Ekspresi yang benar adalah "second only to X in its utility," bukan "into." Preposisi "in" digunakan untuk menjelaskan bidang atau aspek perbandingan.'),
(655, 18, 25, 'The mineral chalcopyrite <span class="error-option" data-label="A">usually is found</span> in compact masses or in mixtures with <span class="error-option" data-label="B">various other mineral</span> as <span class="error-option" data-label="C">opaque, brass-yellow</span>, <span class="error-option" data-label="D">tetragonal crystals</span>.', 'usually is found', 'various other mineral', 'opaque, brass-yellow', 'tetragonal crystals', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Setelah "various other" harus digunakan bentuk jamak: "various other minerals." Karena "other" mengacu pada banyak mineral yang berbeda, bentuk jamak diperlukan.'),
(656, 18, 26, 'Because the study of chemistry <span class="error-option" data-label="A">encompasses</span> the entire material universe, it is central to <span class="error-option" data-label="B">the understand</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="C">of other</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="D">sciences</span>.', 'encompasses', 'the understand', 'of other', 'sciences', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Setelah artikel "the" dibutuhkan nomina: "the understanding of other sciences." "Understand" adalah verba; nomina yang benar adalah "understanding."'),
(657, 18, 27, 'Cyclamates were introduced <span class="error-option" data-label="A">in the early 1950\'s</span> as <span class="error-option" data-label="B">alternative sweeteners</span> for use by individuals <span class="error-option" data-label="C">who needed reducing</span> their sugar intake <span class="error-option" data-label="D">for medical reasons</span>.', 'in the early 1950\'s', 'alternative sweeteners', 'who needed reducing', 'for medical reasons', 'C', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Pola "need + to infinitive" adalah yang benar: individuals who needed to reduce their sugar intake. "Need + -ing" bermakna sesuatu yang perlu dilakukan pada subjek (pasif), bukan oleh subjek.'),
(658, 18, 28, '<span class="error-option" data-label="A">The pericardium</span>, <span class="error-option" data-label="B">a double-layered sac</span>, <span class="error-option" data-label="C">it surrounds</span> the heart and <span class="error-option" data-label="D">the large vessels entering and leaving</span> the heart.', 'The pericardium', 'a double-layered sac', 'it surrounds', 'the large vessels entering and leaving', 'C', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '"it" adalah subjek yang redundan. Kalimat sudah memiliki subjek "The pericardium." Bentuk benar: "The pericardium...surrounds the heart." Menambahkan "it" menciptakan double subject.'),
(659, 18, 29, 'The Hopi, <span class="error-option" data-label="A">descendants of the prehistoric Anasazi people</span>, are <span class="error-option" data-label="B">a Pueblo people</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="C">who of</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="D">the southwestern United States</span>.', 'descendants of the prehistoric Anasazi people', 'a Pueblo people', 'who of', 'the southwestern United States', 'C', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '"who of the southwestern United States" tidak gramatikal karena "who" tidak diikuti verba. Bentuk yang benar adalah "of the southwestern United States" (tanpa "who") atau "who live in the southwestern United States."'),
(660, 18, 30, 'A storyteller <span class="error-option" data-label="A">exercises close control</span> over the storytelling experience <span class="error-option" data-label="B">by the choice of words</span>, <span class="error-option" data-label="C">their arrangement</span>, and <span class="error-option" data-label="D">their effective</span>.', 'exercises close control', 'by the choice of words', 'their arrangement', 'their effective', 'D', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Terdapat paralel struktur: "the choice of words, their arrangement, and their effectiveness." Ketiga frasa membutuhkan nomina. "effective" adalah adjektiva; nomina yang benar adalah "effectiveness."'),
(661, 18, 31, 'Iron is <span class="error-option" data-label="A">one of the basic element</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="B">of which</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="C">the world</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="D">is made</span>.', 'one of the basic element', 'of which', 'the world', 'is made', 'A', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Setelah "one of the" harus digunakan nomina jamak: "one of the basic elements." Ini adalah aturan gramatikal dasar dalam pola "one of the + plural noun."'),
(662, 18, 32, 'The president and vice president are <span class="error-option" data-label="A">the only public officials</span> in <span class="error-option" data-label="B">the United States</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="C">choose in</span> a nationwide election, <span class="error-option" data-label="D">which takes place every four years</span>.', 'the only public officials', 'the United States', 'choose in', 'which takes place every four years', 'C', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Diperlukan bentuk participle pasif untuk memodifikasi "officials": "officials chosen in a nationwide election" (yang dipilih). "Choose" adalah present tense yang salah di sini; bentuk benar adalah "chosen."'),
(663, 18, 33, 'Derived from the concept of natural law is <span class="error-option" data-label="A">the theoretical</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="B">that individuals possess</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="C">inalienable natural rights</span>, as stated in <span class="error-option" data-label="D">the United States Declaration of Independence</span>.', 'the theoretical', 'that individuals possess', 'inalienable natural rights', 'the United States Declaration of Independence', 'A', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Setelah artikel "the" dan sebelum "that" (noun clause), diperlukan nomina. "theory" adalah nomina yang tepat: "the theory that individuals possess..." "theoretical" adalah adjektiva yang tidak bisa berdiri sebagai head noun.'),
(664, 18, 34, 'The United States national debt was <span class="error-option" data-label="A">relatively small</span> until <span class="error-option" data-label="B">the Second World War</span>, <span class="error-option" data-label="C">during when</span> it grew from <span class="error-option" data-label="D">$43 billion to $259 billion</span> in just five years.', 'relatively small', 'the Second World War', 'during when', '$43 billion to $259 billion', 'C', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Setelah preposisi "during" harus digunakan pronoun relatif "which", bukan "when." Bentuk yang benar: "during which it grew from $43 billion..." "when" tidak dapat langsung mengikuti preposisi.'),
(665, 18, 35, 'Brass is stronger than <span class="error-option" data-label="A">either the copper</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="B">and</span> zinc <span class="error-option" data-label="C">of which</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="D">it is composed</span>.', 'either the copper', 'and', 'of which', 'it is composed', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Konjungsi korelatif "either...or" harus berpasangan. "either the copper and zinc" salah; bentuk yang benar adalah "either the copper or zinc."'),
(666, 18, 36, 'In <span class="error-option" data-label="A">the traditional sense</span>, a molecule is <span class="error-option" data-label="B">smallest particle</span> of <span class="error-option" data-label="C">a chemical substance</span> capable of independent existence <span class="error-option" data-label="D">while retaining all of its chemical properties</span>.', 'the traditional sense', 'smallest particle', 'a chemical substance', 'while retaining all of its chemical properties', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Bentuk superlatif harus menggunakan artikel "the": "the smallest particle." Tanpa "the," kalimat tidak gramatikal karena superlatif selalu mengacu pada sesuatu yang spesifik dalam suatu kelompok.'),
(667, 18, 37, 'The <span class="error-option" data-label="A">able</span> of a clarinet to blend and contrast with <span class="error-option" data-label="B">other instruments</span> makes it popular for <span class="error-option" data-label="C">chamber music</span> and <span class="error-option" data-label="D">as a solo instrument</span>.', 'able', 'other instruments', 'chamber music', 'as a solo instrument', 'A', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Diperlukan nomina sebagai head phrase: "The ability of a clarinet to blend..." "able" adalah adjektiva yang tidak bisa berdiri sebagai nomina. Nomina yang benar adalah "ability."'),
(668, 18, 38, 'Phenotypic traits, such as <span class="error-option" data-label="A">size or skin color</span>, <span class="error-option" data-label="B">result to</span> the interaction between <span class="error-option" data-label="C">an organism\'s genetic makeup</span> and <span class="error-option" data-label="D">the environment</span> in which the organism develops.', 'size or skin color', 'result to', 'an organism\'s genetic makeup', 'the environment', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Kolokasi yang benar adalah "result from" (berasal dari / disebabkan oleh): Phenotypic traits result from the interaction... "Result to" bukan ekspresi yang baku dalam bahasa Inggris.'),
(669, 18, 39, '<span class="error-option" data-label="A">To classical scholar</span>, rhetoric was important in <span class="error-option" data-label="B">three spheres</span> of human interaction: in <span class="error-option" data-label="C">law courts</span>, in legislative assemblies, and in <span class="error-option" data-label="D">public forums</span>.', 'To classical scholar', 'three spheres', 'law courts', 'public forums', 'A', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Sebelum singular countable noun "scholar" diperlukan artikel: "To the classical scholar" — atau gunakan bentuk jamak "To classical scholars." Tanpa artikel atau -s, kalimat tidak gramatikal.'),
(670, 18, 40, 'The stark, boxy forms of <span class="error-option" data-label="A">European modernist</span> <span class="error-option" data-label="B">architectural</span> dominated <span class="error-option" data-label="C">United States cityscapes</span> in the building boom <span class="error-option" data-label="D">following the Second World War</span>.', 'European modernist', 'architectural', 'United States cityscapes', 'following the Second World War', 'B', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', '2026-04-06 01:58:30', 'Setelah "modernist" diperlukan nomina sebagai head: "forms of European modernist architecture." "architectural" adalah adjektiva yang tidak dapat berdiri sebagai nomina di sini. Bentuk nomina yang benar adalah "architecture."');
INSERT INTO `users` (`id`, `name`, `email`, `email_verified_at`, `password`, `remember_token`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `role`, `status`, `profile_photo`, `is_admin`, `class_period_id`, `phone_number`, `teacher_id`, `program_id`, `bio`, `learning_mode`, `referral_code`, `referred_by_id`, `referral_points`, `utm_source`, `utm_medium`, `utm_campaign`, `utm_content`, `utm_term`, `acquisition_referrer`, `acquisition_landing_path`, `acquisition_source_page`, `acquisition_variant`, `acquisition_last_cta`) VALUES
